    "knowledge_point": 17592186059820,
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sin\\left(x+\\pi\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\sin(u+v)=\\sin u\\cos v+\\cos u\\sin v.\n$$\n\nThe fixed angle has exact values\n\n$$\n\\cos\\left(\\pi\\right)=-1,\\qquad \\sin\\left(\\pi\\right)=0.\n$$\n\nSubstitute $u=x$ and $v=\\pi$, then simplify the coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin\\left(x+\\pi\\right)&=\\sin x\\cos\\left(\\pi\\right)+\\cos x\\sin\\left(\\pi\\right)\\\\\n&=\\sin x\\left(-1\\right)+\\cos x\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\sin x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/easy"
      },
